1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,529
Lucia burned their map at the
waterfront. Jason watched their escape

2
00:00:04,529 --> 00:00:07,000
route turn black between her fingers.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,250
Earlier, he had found it tucked beneath
their motel door. A shortcut

4
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:14,000
through the cargo yards.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,688
The handwriting looked familiar. So did
the coffee stain. This was the map

6
00:00:19,688 --> 00:00:21,000
they had lost.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,056
Someone had returned it with a new route
drawn across the center. Jason

8
00:00:26,056 --> 00:00:28,000
nearly followed the fresh arrows.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,118
Lucia held it against the window.
Original pencil marks continued

10
00:00:32,118 --> 00:00:35,000
underneath, past a gate marked
permanently closed.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,444
The new route led them into that dead
end. Whoever found the map was

12
00:00:40,444 --> 00:00:42,000
waiting for them there.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,053
Back at the waterfront, Jason unfolded
the ferry timetable instead. Public

14
00:00:46,053 --> 00:00:49,000
lights. Open water. No shortcut through
silent containers.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,158
Lucia dropped the last burned corner
into a metal ashtray. They had lost a

16
00:00:54,158 --> 00:00:56,000
map, and kept their exit.
